<p>On LongBench, the method achieves 34.59 average score on Dream-7B and 37.02 on UltraLLaDA — both state-of-the-art. Notably, adding intra-chunk token sparsity (top-B token selection within each chosen chunk) improves accuracy from 22.01 to 34.59 on Dream-7B, contrary to the degradation observed in AR LLMs under sparse attention. The bidirectional nature of dLLM attention benefits from token pruning because the most query-relevant tokens are retained with high fidelity.</p>

<h3>Chunk size ablation</h3>
<p>The chunk size C controls the granularity of retrieval. Keeping the total token budget fixed (K × C = 4096), smaller chunks with more selections (C=256, K=16) outperform larger chunks at very long contexts (128K): 92.3% EM vs 83.0% for C=1024. At moderate lengths (16K–32K), C=1024, K=4 is optimal. The key insight: finer granularity lets the retrieval score be more precise, which matters most when there are many irrelevant chunks to sift through.</p>
